  "slug": "self-supervised-few-labels-digits",
  "direction": "Does self-supervised pretraining help when labels are scarce, at tiny scale? On the scikit-learn 8x8 digits images, pretrain a small CNN encoder with (a) rotation prediction and (b) a SimCLR-style contrastive loss with small augmentations, then train a linear probe with 10, 50 and 200 labels. Compare against supervised training from scratch on the same labels and against PCA features plus logistic regression.",
